{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}","id":1019164,"title":"Useful [1E] Forsaken Books for running [2E}","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-19T04:51:53-08:00","id":1019164,"title":"Useful [1E] Forsaken Books for running [2E}","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> Starting my first CoD Chronicle in the new year for Werewolf. Considering the big sale on Drivethru for the Holiday Season I was looking at maybe picking up some of the 1E titles while they're more pocket friendly. I've already looked at the recommendations from the 2E Core book itself and definitely feel I should pick up a copy of The Pack. I was hoping some of the more experienced Story Tellers might be able to point me in the right direction of what might be useful as I'm not sure what the extent of the changes between 1E &amp; 2E. My group is relatively new to CoD and have only played a few seasons of VtR 1E if that is of any help.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7354-monsieurcutts","name":"MonsieurCutts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T07:51:59-08:00","id":1019222,"title":"","content":"Hm, the setting changes between 1E and 2E are a bit more pronounced than in Vampire. I picked up a bunch of 1E books leading up to 2E's release and most of them lost some usefulness. That being said, if you're also getting The Pack and need some more ideas for Lodges, you can use the ones described in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3072/Lodges-The-Faithful\" target=\"_blank\">Lodges: The Faithful</a>, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/15819/Lodges-The-Splintered\" target=\"_blank\">Lodges: The Splintered</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55598/Tribes-of-the-Moon\" target=\"_blank\">Tribes of the Moon</a>.<br /> <br /> Tribes of the Moon will also give you an overview of the Tribes, but it'll be missing their focus on their Favored Prey from 2E. That being said, if you want to showcase the Shadow you should pick up <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/Predators\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a> since it focuses primarily on Spirits and Hosts.<br /> <br /> See, that's really the biggest issue: the books I'm most excited to recommend for 1E are ones that added something major to the setting: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3418/Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">Blasphemies</a>, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/23681/The-Pure\" target=\"_blank\">The Pure</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/25702/The-War-Against-the-Pure\" target=\"_blank\">War Against the Pure</a> are all fantastic books. But they'll just make things more complicated at the beginning. And since the enemies in those three books are chiefly other werewolves, most of the Gifts and such are gonna be a pain because you'll have to ditch all of that stuff entirely due to how Gifts work in 2E.<br /> <br /> It's neither on sale nor a Werewolf-specific book, but <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28796/Damnation-City\" target=\"_blank\">Damnation City</a> is probably the best thing supplement from the entirety of 1E for any gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T08:00:09-08:00","id":1019229,"title":"","content":"I am running a Werewolf 2E chronicle based on the old demo for 1E &quot;Manitou Springs&quot; and found both the demo and the book on the rockies (Hunting Ground: The Rockies) very helpful. Especially in the demo you have to tweak a little beforehand, cause some mechanics work very differently in 2E, but it was a great source for the general szenario and story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:04:40-08:00","id":1019697,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your responses both I'll definitely check out your recommendations. I spotted there's a Storyteller's Screen for First Edition is this still useful for running Forsaken in it's latest incarnation? Do you find any particular area's that you reference a lot in actual play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7354-monsieurcutts","name":"MonsieurCutts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T03:53:10-08:00","id":1020260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1019222#post1019222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, the setting changes between 1E and 2E are a bit more pronounced than in Vampire. I picked up a bunch of 1E books leading up to 2E's release and most of them lost some usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly changed? I thought 2e was fully backward-compatible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:10:07-08:00","id":1020297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020260#post1020260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly changed? I thought 2e was fully backward-compatible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts are completely different for one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:00:39-08:00","id":1020367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020297#post1020297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gifts are completely different for one thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a review somewhere that breaks down the differences and how they affect using 1e sources with 2e rules or vice versa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:10:58-08:00","id":1020428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020367#post1020367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a review somewhere that breaks down the differences and how they affect using 1e sources with 2e rules or vice versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. Most of the stuff you would use from first edition would be spirits and fluff, which hasn't changed much and there's not much need for a conversion guide.<br /> <br /> A more comprehensive list of differences was made out <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/4tu0da/werewolf_forsaken_1st_ed_vs_2nd/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. There's probably a few on the forum but I don't know where they are.<br /> <br /> Going past Gifts and Rites, which have changed a lot along with Merits, just with regular character sheets you won't have much of a difference. The big change there would be adding Athletics to Defense and probably changing the stats of various weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:18:52-08:00","id":1020434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020367#post1020367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a review somewhere that breaks down the differences and how they affect using 1e sources with 2e rules or vice versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one that breaks down the differences but I can't link it, it's unapproved. There's nothing that really goes into the details of conversion, or a conversion guide.<br /> <br /> The big thing you would be able to bring over would be spirits and fluff, which has for the most part stayed the same, or at least similar.<br /> <br /> If you're just transferring character stats over, past the Gifts, Rites and Merits which have changed, the only bigthings you would really have to do would be add Athletics to Defense and fiddle with some weapon stats. There's probably some other minor changes as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:52:07-08:00","id":1020454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020260#post1020260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly changed? I thought 2e was fully backward-compatible?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious as to where you got that impression? <br /> <br /> And also, what does 'fully backward-compatible' actually mean in the context of an edition change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:52:24-08:00","id":1020456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020434#post1020434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's one that breaks down the differences but I can't link it, it's unapproved.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUnapproved? By who?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:47:54-08:00","id":1020493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1020456#post1020456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bUnapproved? By who?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. I realized after I posted that posts with reddit links are automatically put into an Unapproved stasis. I guess I got approved after the fact, however.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T06:22:19-08:00","id":1022297,"title":"","content":"Thanks much for the link. Very useful indeed. It seems that the changes are almost all on the PC side, which is encouraging, as was hoping to use stuff from some of the older sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> What gave me the impression that 1e and 2e were the same? Just not paying attention, really. The focus has always seemed to be the choice between cWoD and nWoD rather than between different editions of nWoD......which we seem to have three of now :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T15:37:56-08:00","id":1022484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1022297#post1022297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What gave me the impression that 1e and 2e were the same? Just not paying attention, really. The focus has always seemed to be the choice between cWoD and nWoD rather than between different editions of nWoD......which we seem to have three of now :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are four editions of WoD, and two editions of CofD (not sure why you'd think there's three).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:45:15-08:00","id":1022551,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the God-Machine rules update confused the matter since it contains second edition rules before the second edition was officially announced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T07:57:45-08:00","id":1022759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1022551#post1022551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the God-Machine rules update confused the matter since it contains second edition rules before the second edition was officially announced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I had thought the God-Machine rules update came later, as a kind of 2.5 rules update. So there are only two versions? That's good news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:48:21-08:00","id":1027264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1022297#post1022297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks much for the link. Very useful indeed. It seems that the changes are almost all on the PC side, which is encouraging, as was hoping to use stuff from some of the older sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> What gave me the impression that 1e and 2e were the same? Just not paying attention, really. The focus has always seemed to be the choice between cWoD and nWoD rather than between different editions of nWoD......which we seem to have three of now :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, ok. Just curious since it seemed pretty clear. But yeah the whole WoD verses CofD (formerly nWod) thing is pretty confusing for a lot of people so I can see missing the CofD edition change details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:52:49-08:00","id":1027451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1019164-useful-1e-forsaken-books-for-running-2e}?p=1022759#post1022759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I had thought the God-Machine rules update came later, as a kind of 2.5 rules update. So there are only two versions? That's good news.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the story: the old license holders didn't want an official edition change but did allow a rules update that was a new edition in all but name, so rather than second editions we got &quot;chronicle books&quot; that were basically exactly that. Mortals didn't have a full new corebook coming, so instead they got the G-M update as a patch 1.5 update to the new rules. Then things changed, 2e got okayed, and the rest is history.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine Rules Update is a relic from a time when there was a new edition but nobody could call it that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}